00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
Original story by Johanna Spyri

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
<b>Alps no Shoujo Heidi</b>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
<u>Why do I hear</u>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
Kuchibue ha naze

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
<u>the whistling from far away?</u>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
<u>Why is that cloud</u>

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
Ano kumo ha naze

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
<u>waiting for me?</u>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
Watashi wo matteru no

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
<u>Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm.</u>

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.600
The Whisper of The Firs

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:45.340
<i>It's been three months since
Heidi came to Alm Mountain</i>

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.430
<i>to live with her grandfather.</i>

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.550
<i>And now, summer is coming to an end.</i>

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.010
<i>Heidi has become accustomed
to life on the mountain,</i>

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:57.850
<i>and she has now become
very good at milking the goats.</i>

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.300
<i>She has also learned to whistle.</i>

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:08.420
<i>Heidi has already become
a child of the mountain.</i>

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.630
Pichi, it's time to eat!

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.110
<i>Pichi was only a chick when Heidi found him.</i>

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.970
<i>All too soon, he's become a full grown bird.</i>

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.740
Little Swan!

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.250
Now, stand still until I've finished.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.290
You do it very well.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.360
I'm almost finished.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.950
I'm going to eat!

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:09.320
Peter, shouldn't we take the goats
home, before it starts raining?

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.320
Raining?

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:13.930
It won't rain, so don't worry!

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.950
But look at those clouds!

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:23.020
Those clouds don't bring rain.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:28.440
The goats are quiet, aren't they?

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:38.710
It's just the wind in the sky!

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.730
Oh, I see.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.410
Then we don't need to worry.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.840
Peter, I'm a hawk!

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.810
It's a cloud, Peter! A cloud!

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:31.170
Peter, I'm in the middle of a cloud!
Everything is white!

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.520
Heidi, be careful!

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.230
What is it, Peter?

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:38.140
Heidi!

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.030
What's wrong, Peter?

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:46.100
What do you mean "what's wrong"?
You almost fell in the ravine!

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.930
It's wonderful!

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:05.970
Well, let's eat.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:22.940
Goodbye!

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.350
Goodbye! I'll see you tomorrow!

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:27.330
Grandfather, I'm back!

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:29.790
Welcome back. Were you cold?

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.400
No, I was all right.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:35.360
Today something very
amusing happened on the mountain, Grandfather!

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:42.530
I was milking a goat and then, suddenly,
a strong wind made me fall on my back.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:50.090
The wind was amazing. I tried to get up,
but it pushed me back. I couldn't move.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.000
That is very dangerous.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.600
But playing with the wind was very fun.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.240
Grandfather, let me do that.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.360
Then, I'm counting on you.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.450
You do it very well!

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:19.410
Really?

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.340
Yes.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:27.850
Heidi, you can't go to the mountains tomorrow.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:29.510
Oh? Why not?

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:34.490
Because autumn is coming and
the wind is becoming stronger.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.740
The wind today was just a warning.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:40.960
If a small girl like you go up the mountain,

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:44.050
you can easily be blown over the edge
and into the ravine by the wind.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.770
The wind didn't hurt me.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:51.870
It just pushed me so that I
could run with the clouds.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:54.660
I felt like a hawk.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:01.120
If I had kept running, I could have
jumped to the other side of the ravine.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:02.120
Ravine?

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:07.180
Yes. I could not see it because of the cloud.
I stopped just in time.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.170
Well, I can go, can't I?

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.720
It's best that you don't go, after all.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.440
Pichi, good morning.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.490
Grandfather, good morning!

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:41.290
Good morning!

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:42.290
Good morning!

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:51.200
Grandfather!

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.460
What is it?

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.690
I really can't go to the mountains?

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.720
No, it's best that you don't go.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.760
But there is no wind today.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:04.840
Look how quiet the fir trees are.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:17.560
It's still morning, so they're quiet for now,
but later the wind will start to blow.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:23.970
Really?

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.020
Yes.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.280
Good morning, Snowflake!

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.360
Good morning, Greenfinch!

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:42.810
Heidi, good morning.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:44.340
Good morning!

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:49.050
I'm sorry, everyone.
I can't come with you to the mountain.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:50.880
Why not?

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.500
Grandfather says the wind will
get stronger, so I can't go.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.890
Now, off you go!

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.340
Are you all right with that?

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:03.170
Come on, everyone!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.260
You have to hurry and go!

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:10.720
Stop that, Greenfinch!

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.340
Everyone, go!

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:14.440
What's wrong?

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.820
Grandfather, why can't I go to the mountains?

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.250
Stop it.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.380
If I don't go, Snowflake and
the others don't want to go either.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.400
Can I?

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:31.770
It's best that you don't go.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:39.100
And, Heidi, if you stay in the house,
I will teach you how to make cheese.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:40.700
Really?

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:41.810
Yes.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.030
I've wanted to learn to
make it for a long time.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:48.490
Peter, I can't go, after all.
I'm going to make cheese.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:52.450
Now, everyone get along!

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:53.600
Hey, don't go that way!

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:56.980
This way! Hurry up and come!

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:02.020
Snowflake!

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:04.950
Come!

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:14.160
<i>Peter feels lonely because Heidi
won't come with him up the mountain.</i>

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:17.350
<i>Suddenly, he's in a bad mood.</i>

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:20.860
<i>And the goats, who are used
to having Heidi around,</i>

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:23.320
<i>and are calm when she is there,</i>

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:27.370
<i>become unruly and won't listen to Peter.</i>

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:34.600
Grandfather, teach me.
How do we make cheese?

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:37.650
First we have to light the fire.

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:43.320
Greenfinch, don't stay behind.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:46.380
Stop!

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:47.650
Come on, stop!

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:50.840
You rascal! Damn it!

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:52.780
Crap.

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:56.290
Snowflake!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.220
Where are you going?
Come back here!

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.170
Why you...

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:10.270
Heidi, you idiot.
This is because you didn't come.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:33.460
Grandfather, the wind began to blow!

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.970
Didn't I tell you?

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:48.090
Grandfather, what is that sound?

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:51.780
It's the wind blowing though
the fir trees at the back.

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:42.000
<i>Heidi listens to the strong winds roaring
through the branches of the fir trees.</i>

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:46.800
<i>All the while, the trees continue to make sounds.</i>

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:49.800
<i>They seem to be speaking of something,</i>

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:52.660
<i>and Heidi is fascinated.</i>

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:00.470
Heidi, what are you doing out here?

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.060
I'm listening to the sound of the firs.

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:09.230
Do you like the sound
of the fir trees that much?

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:09.960
Yes.

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:12.480
It's like they are talking.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:15.760
I see.

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:18.400
In the autumn, the winds are
usually this strong up here.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.610
You'll be able to hear it often.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:21.980
Really?

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:23.520
Really.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:26.910
Come on. Don't keep standing
in a place like this.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.700
Hurry and come inside so we
can start making cheese.

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:30.650
Yes.

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:38.630
What do we do when you've
poured the milk into the pot?

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:42.600
Now we have to heat the milk and stir it well.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:44.380
And then the cheese will be ready?

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:46.730
Of course not.

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.650
We still have much to do.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:50.980
What are we going to do?

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.750
You will see.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.700
Grandfather, where is my spoon?

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:09.670
What?

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:15.430
The spoon for me to stir
the milk. Where is it?

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.430
I see.

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:19.030
Well, you can just watch.

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:22.280
You said I could help you!

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.520
Huh? Well...

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.090
I'll do it well. Give it to me!

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.490
Can you really do it?

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.490
I can do it, I really can.

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:31.710
Then, here it is.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:35.420
Are you all right?

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:36.830
I'm all right.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.780
You do it well.

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:03.480
Well, in the meantime, perhaps I
should hurry and bring in the hay.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:04.480
All right.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:08.960
I see. Well, Heidi, keep on stirring
so that it doesn't get burned.

00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:09.870
Yes.

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:19.300
Grandfather?

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:33.300
That's not the sound of the firs.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.020
Who's there?

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:18.840
Snowflake!

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.760
You're back already?

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:25.300
You're back earlier.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.800
Peter, welcome back!

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:52.340
Snowflake, you came down from
the mountain alone, didn't you?

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:58.560
What a troublesome kid! If you go
down alone, Peter will be worried!

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:01.090
I'm sure that he is looking for you!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:05.740
Well, we can't leave Peter worried. Let's go!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.400
Snowflake! Snowflake!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:24.090
Snowflake!

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:26.260
Snowflake!

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.450
Snowflake!

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:34.890
Heidi!

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:36.180
Peter!

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:37.430
Snowflake.

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:40.660
I brought her back to you!

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:46.410
You promised that you wouldn't beat them!
And Snowflake is still small!

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:51.250
I know that, but Alm-Uncle said that I
should beat them if they leave the herd!

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:52.490
Grandfather said that?

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:55.110
Why you... Take that!

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:02.080
It's because you...
It's because you spoiled them!

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:00.790
Grandfather, I'm sorry.

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:05.750
Snowflake came back alone...
So I...

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:10.470
Don't worry, Heidi.
It's Grandfather's fault.

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:20.810
I should have known it was
impossible for you to do such a thing.

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:30.190
We'll try to make cheese again tomorrow.
Today...

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:52.260
<i>Grandfather doesn't scold Heidi.</i>

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:55.870
<i>However, Heidi feels very sad.</i>

00:20:56.370 --> 00:21:00.860
<i>Heidi feels she should have
been able to stir the milk.</i>

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:03.790
<i>It wasn't impossible at all.</i>

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:09.560
<i>But Snowflake had distracted her,
and she had burned the milk.</i>

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:15.880
<i>If she had been more strict with
the goats, like Peter had said,</i>

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:18.040
<i>perhaps this wouldn't have happened.</i>

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:31.770
<i>The fir trees seem to be telling her:</i>

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:34.850
<i>Heidi, do you understand?</i>

00:21:34.990 --> 00:21:37.780
<i>You won't fail tomorrow,
so don't give up.</i>

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:42.620
<i>You'll see that Grandfather will let
you help making cheese again.</i>

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:45.240
You think so?

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:55.030
Heidi.

00:21:55.730 --> 00:21:56.960
What's wrong?

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.240
I'm listening to what the firs are saying.

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:01.630
All right, all right.

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:06.530
Grandfather, will you let me help you clean the pot?

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:07.180
Yes.

00:22:23.010 --> 00:22:25.210
Good morning, Peter!

00:22:25.580 --> 00:22:26.730
Good morning!

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:29.410
Go on, go with him.

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:31.200
Hurry up and go!

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:36.320
Snowflake!

00:22:38.090 --> 00:22:40.850
Snowflake, go or I'll beat you!

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:42.130
Heidi!

00:22:42.540 --> 00:22:46.250
A white kid goat

00:22:42.540 --> 00:22:46.250
Masshirona koyagi

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:43.560
Go!

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:48.240
Then I'll see you later.

00:22:47.070 --> 00:22:50.430
Your name is Yuki

00:22:47.070 --> 00:22:50.430
Namae ha yuki

00:22:48.670 --> 00:22:50.480
Be careful!

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:55.590
The first time

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:55.590
Itsuka shira hajimete

00:22:56.060 --> 00:23:00.050
I met you

00:22:56.060 --> 00:23:00.050
Anata to deatta no ha

00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:03.710
<i>That day, Heidi helps Grandfather make cheese.</i>

00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:04.000
That's right.

00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:04.000
Sou ne

00:23:04.290 --> 00:23:06.530
<i>Living in the mountains can be hard.</i>

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:11.600
It was at that spring

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:11.600
Ano izumi no hotori

00:23:06.620 --> 00:23:10.160
<i>Heidi has learned that from yesterday's incident.</i>

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:14.300
<i>That's why she has sent Snowflake away.</i>

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:22.090
that we both drank of the cool water

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:22.090
Tsumetai mizu wo issho ni nonda hi

00:23:14.720 --> 00:23:19.440
<i>This is how Heidi will learn things,
one at a time.</i>

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:24.670
That's right.

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:24.670
Sou ne

00:23:25.530 --> 00:23:31.860
It was at that spring

00:23:25.530 --> 00:23:31.860
Ano izumi no hotori

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:43.850
that we both drank of the cool water

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:43.850
Tsumetai mizu wo issho ni nonda hi

00:23:57.550 --> 00:24:01.070
<i>Fall has come to Alm Mountain.</i>

00:24:01.070 --> 00:24:04.750
<i>Every day is a joy to Heidi who has
become a child of the mountain.</i>

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:08.860
<i>One day, Pichi, who always wakes
her in the morning, is gone.</i>

00:24:09.150 --> 00:24:11.730
<i>Heidi is worried, and decides to
go up the mountain</i>

00:24:11.730 --> 00:24:14.120
<i>to see if she can find Pichi.</i>

00:24:14.260 --> 00:24:17.630
<i>She calls for Pichi, but he doesn't come.</i>

00:24:17.630 --> 00:24:20.700
<i>Seeing that Heidi is very sad,</i>

00:24:20.700 --> 00:24:24.250
<i>Grandfather takes her
with him to pick chestnuts.</i>

00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:27.610
<i>Next episode:
Where have you gone, Pichi?</i>

00:24:27.610 --> 00:24:29.610
<i>Please look forward to it!</i>

00:24:32.440 --> 00:24:36.420
Web Master    Cyber Zero

00:24:32.440 --> 00:24:36.420
Styler    Cyber Zero

00:24:32.440 --> 00:24:36.420
Karaoke    Cyber Zero

